# Simple example as seen in the "How CG3 enables dependency parsing" section of the overview. Tags only contain POS information.

# Define tags (so brackets don't have to be used in rules)
LIST N = N ;
LIST V = V ;
LIST PRON = PRON ;
LIST DET = DET ;

# Dependency tags to be added
LIST det = @det ;
LIST nsubj = @nsubj ;
LIST obj = @obj ;


### Rules to parse dependency links

# Assign Determiner
SETPARENT DET  TO (1 N) ; # If a noun is preceded by a determiner, set noun as parent to determiner.

# Assign Subject
SETPARENT PRON  TO (1 V) ; # If verb is preceded by a pronoun, set verb as parent to noun.

# Assign Object
SETPARENT N IF (-1 DET) TO (-2 V) ; # If a noun is preceded by a determiner, and two words to the left is a verb, set verb as parent of the noun.


### Rules to assign relationship labels (same order as dependency rules above)

# Determiner relation
ADD det DET IF (1 N) ; # Add Determiner relation tag

# Subject relation
ADD nsubj PRON IF (1 V) ; # Add Subject relation tag

# Object relation
ADD obj N IF (-1 DET) (-2 V) ; # Add Object relation tag